<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<SettingsBlock>
  <ModSettings Class="LootScavenging.LootScavengingSettings">
    <activePreset>Progression</activePreset>

    <!-- How this file works.
         Auto Mod Config copies this file into the game's Config folder, replacing the player's saved Loot Scavenging settings.
         The file name is Mod_<install folder>_LootScavengingMod.xml. This one is for a copy in a folder named "Loot Scavenging".
         A key left out takes the default in the mod's Defs/SettingsDefaults.xml, which is the Progression preset unless a
         modpack patched it. So a file may hold only the keys you change. A file that names the Cleanup preset and two keys
         does not give Cleanup's rows: list those rows too, or write a full file.
         A setting a modpack locks always ends at the pack's value, whatever this file says.
         Do not write defaultsSeeded. The mod sets it.
         Booleans are true or false. Enum values are written exactly as listed. Fractions are 0 to 1.

         activePreset: Progression, Cleanup, Vanilla. It only sets which preset the settings page names. The values below
           decide what the mod does.

         Who and when
           hostile, nonHostileFaction, noFaction, prisoners: true, false (which groups' gear is sorted)
           homeMapOnly: true, false
           onDownedAndStrip: true, false (also sort when a pawn is downed or stripped, not only at death)
         What out-of-reach gear becomes
           dropMode: ScrapOutOfReach, ScrapEverything, KeepOriginal, Off
           dropIncludesMedicine: true, false
           dropIncludesAmmunition: true, false
           deathDrop: Ground, ScrapOnBody, AllOnBody
           eraFallback: CarrierFaction, ColonyEra, Components
         One rule per category. Replace <category> with weapons, apparel, ammunition, drugs, medicine, food or other,
         which gives for example weaponsOutcome and apparelBelowQuality (49 keys in all).
           <category>Outcome: Keep, Degrade, Scrap, Disassemble, Delete
           <category>OnlyBeyondReach: true, false
           <category>LimitQuality: true, false
           <category>BelowQuality: Awful, Poor, Normal, Good, Excellent, Masterwork, Legendary
           <category>LimitHitPoints: true, false
           <category>BelowHitPointFraction: 0.05 to 1
           <category>Chance: 0 to 1
         Degrade, disassemble and charges
           degradeMin, degradeMax: 0.01 to 1
           degradeLowersQuality: true, false
           disassemblyYield: EraTypical, ItemBased
           disassemblyEfficiency: 0.05 to 1
           ejectCharges: true, false
         Protection and lists
           protectQuestItems, protectUniqueWeapons, protectPersonaWeapons, protectRelics: true, false
           keepList, removeList: item def names, as <keepList><li>Gun_Revolver</li></keepList>
         Corpses
           corpseHumanlike, corpseAnimal, corpseMechanoid: true, false
           corpseChance: 0 to 1
           butcherRemovesApparel: true, false
         Scrap, study and recycling
           scrapMarketValue: 0.01 to 10
           unfamiliarScope: AllOutOfReach, LootedOnly
           studyEras: ColonyEraAndBelow, AnyEra
           recycleOrStudy: OneOrTheOther, StudyThenRecycle
           studyTechprintProjects: true, false
           studyPointsNeolithic, studyPointsMedieval, studyPointsIndustrial, studyPointsSpacer, studyPointsUltra,
             studyPointsArchotech: 0 to 1000 (research points per unit; 0 stops that scrap being studied)
           studyPointsMultiplier: 0 to 3 (scales every tier's points) -->
  </ModSettings>
</SettingsBlock>
